<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Training Algorithm</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Grace</span>: Generative Representation Learning via Contrastive Policy Optimization</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Training data <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(q_{i},d_{i}^{+},d_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(q_{i},d_{i}^{+},d_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, Initial policy <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Hyperparameters: rollouts <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, coefficients <math id="alg1.l0a.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0b" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Fine-tuned policy <math id="alg1.l0b.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with enhanced representation capabilities

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> epoch <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{epochs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>epochs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{epochs}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> batch <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}=\{(q_{i},d_{i}^{+},d_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}=\{(q_{i},d_{i}^{+},d_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{B}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Phase 1: Generate interpretable rationale via policy</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">in parallel</span> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
                Generate query rationale: <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{q_{i}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{q_{i}}=</annotation></semantics></math>r<math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(q_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(q_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
                Generate negative rationale: <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{d_{i}^{-}}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{-}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{d_{i}^{-}}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{-}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
                Sample <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> positive rationale: <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{+}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{+}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Phase 2: Extract semantic representations via masked pooling</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
               Encode all rationale: <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{P}(x)\oplus y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{P}(x)\oplus y)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
               Apply masked mean pooling (Eq. <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.2 From Rationale to Representation ‣ 3 Generative Representation Learning via Contrastive Policy Optimization ‣ Grace: Generative Representation Learning via Contrastive Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>):

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
                <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{-}},\{\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}\leftarrow\text{MaskedPool}(\mathbf{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>MaskedPool</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{-}},\{\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}\leftarrow\text{MaskedPool}(\mathbf{E})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Phase 3: Compute multi-dimensional contrastive rewards</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
                Identify hard negatives: <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{i}=\{j\neq i:\max_{l}\text{sim}(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext>sim</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{i}=\{j\neq i:\max_{l}\text{sim}(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)})\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}=\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\big)-\sum_{m=1}^{M_{i}}\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i,m}^{-}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.521em;" width="1.521em"><mtext>sim</mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.521em;" width="1.521em"><mtext>sim</mtext></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}=\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}\big)-\sum_{m=1}^{M_{i}}\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i,m}^{-}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}=\frac{1}{K-1}\sum_{j\neq k}\text{sim}(\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(j)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>consist</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}=\frac{1}{K-1}\sum_{j\neq k}\text{sim}(\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)},\mathbf{h}_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(j)})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}=-\frac{1}{B-1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j=1\\
j\neq i\end{subarray}}^{B}\max_{\,1\leq l\leq K}\,\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>hard</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>B</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:1.521em;" width="1.521em"><mtext>sim</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}=-\frac{1}{B-1}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}j=1\\
j\neq i\end{subarray}}^{B}\max_{\,1\leq l\leq K}\,\text{sim}\!\big(\mathbf{h}_{q_{i}},\mathbf{h}_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i,k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>consist</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>hard</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i,k)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{R}}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}/{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{R}}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}/{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
              
              
                <span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// Phase 4: Optimize policy via GRPO</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
              
              
               Compute group baseline: <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
              
              
               Compute advantages: <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}-b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(i,k)}=\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}-b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
              
              
               Update policy: <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta+\alpha\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta+\alpha\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> where

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
              
              
                <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{GRPO}}=\sum_{i,k}A^{(i,k)}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{+}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{GRPO}}=\sum_{i,k}A^{(i,k)}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|\mathcal{P}(d_{i}^{+}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  Optimized policy <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Theoretical Perspective Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework establishes a principled connection between contrastive learning and reinforcement learning, leveraging their shared ability to learn from feedback rather than absolute ground truth labels. This fundamental similarity enables a natural integration of their objectives.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Unified Learning Without Ground Truth</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both contrastive learning and reinforcement learning operate on comparative signals: contrastive learning distinguishes positive from negative samples, while reinforcement learning optimizes based on rewards signals. This parallel allows us to reformulate the contrastive objective as a reward signal:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{CL}}=-\log\frac{\exp(\text{sim}(q,d^{+}))}{\sum_{d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{D}}\exp(\text{sim}(q,d^{\prime}))}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathcal{R}=\text{sim}(q,d^{+})-\sum_{d^{-}\in\mathcal{D}^{-}}\text{sim}(q,d^{-})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{CL}}=-\log\frac{\exp(\text{sim}(q,d^{+}))}{\sum_{d^{\prime}\in\mathcal{D}}\exp(\text{sim}(q,d^{\prime}))}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathcal{R}=\text{sim}(q,d^{+})-\sum_{d^{-}\in\mathcal{D}^{-}}\text{sim}(q,d^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This transformation enables policy gradient optimization without requiring explicit labels, only relative preferences encoded in the contrastive structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Connection to InfoNCE</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework can be understood as implicitly optimizing a generative variant of the InfoNCE objective. Consider the expected reward under our multi-faceted design:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}}[\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>consist</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>hard</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}}[\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}^{(i,k)}+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding the contrastive learning component:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}=\log\frac{p(y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}{p(y_{d_{i}^{-}}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}^{(i,k)}=\log\frac{p(y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}{p(y_{d_{i}^{-}}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With hard negative mining across the batch:</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}=-\log\left(\frac{1}{B-1}\sum_{j\neq i}^{B}\max_{l}p(y_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>hard</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>l</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}^{(i)}=-\log\left(\frac{1}{B-1}\sum_{j\neq i}^{B}\max_{l}p(y_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Combining these terms, the expected total reward approximates:</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}]\propto\log\frac{p(d^{+}|q,\pi_{\theta})}{p(d^{-}|q,\pi_{\theta})\cdot\prod_{j\neq i}\max_{l}p(y_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}+\lambda_{1}\mathbb{E}[\text{consistency}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>consistency</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{R}_{\text{total}}]\propto\log\frac{p(d^{+}|q,\pi_{\theta})}{p(d^{-}|q,\pi_{\theta})\cdot\prod_{j\neq i}\max_{l}p(y_{d_{j}^{+}}^{(l)}|q_{i},\pi_{\theta})}+\lambda_{1}\mathbb{E}[\text{consistency}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.3 </span>Convergence Analysis</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization landscape of our framework benefits from the variance reduction properties of both contrastive learning and policy gradient optimization. The consistency reward acts as a regularizer, bounding the policy updates:</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|\leq C\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}\|+\lambda_{1}\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}\|+\lambda_{2}\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}\|\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>CL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>consist</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>hard</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|\leq C\cdot\mathbb{E}\left[\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{CL}}\|+\lambda_{1}\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}\|+\lambda_{2}\|\mathcal{R}_{\text{hard}}\|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant dependent on the policy parameterization. The consistency term <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>consist</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{\text{consist}}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}-y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(j)}\|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}-y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(j)}\|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, preventing divergent interpretations and ensuring stable convergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This theoretical foundation reveals that our approach maintains the discriminative power of contrastive learning while unleashing the generative capabilities of LLMs, enabling the policy to actively interpret and understand text rather than merely discriminate between samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.4 </span>Additional Training Details</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We incorporate length regularization to prevent degenerate solutions where the model generates excessively long responses without meaningful content:</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{final}}^{(i,k)}=\begin{cases}\hat{\mathcal{R}}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}&amp;\text{if }|y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|&lt;L_{\max}\text{ or }y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}[-1]=\text{EOS}\\
-\gamma&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>final</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>total</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>EOS</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{final}}^{(i,k)}=\begin{cases}\hat{\mathcal{R}}_{\text{total}}^{(i,k)}&amp;\text{if }|y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}|&lt;L_{\max}\text{ or }y_{d_{i}^{+}}^{(k)}[-1]=\text{EOS}\\
-\gamma&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum allowed sequence length and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a penalty coefficient for over-length generations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.5 </span>Additional Implementation Details</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training uses the AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter (2019)</a></cite> optimizer with a fixed learning rate of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> and no warmup schedule. The maximum prompt length is set to 1024 tokens and the maximum response length to 2048 tokens, with over-length sequences truncated on the right side. A length penalty <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> is applied when responses reach the maximum length without emitting an EOS token. For GRPO, we generate <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=8</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts per positive document using temperature sampling with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, and compute advantages relative to a mean baseline without normalization. The consistency weight <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, and the hard negative weight <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>. The scaling <math id="A1.SS2.SSS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for our training is set to 10. Multi-GPU training is managed with Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2023)</a></cite>, with parameter and optimizer state sharding to alleviate memory constraints. Training-time generation leverages vLLM <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm</a></span></span></span> with tensor-parallel size 2 and 50% GPU memory utilization in eager mode for stability. Instruction tokens are automatically detected and excluded from pooling operations to prevent contamination in representation extraction. At inference time, we adopt the same generation and pooling configurations as training to ensure consistency.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
